\title{(Simple) graph}
\date{2026-09-13T03:39:43Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\taxon{Definition}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{A (simple) \em{graph} #{G = (V, E)} is a set of \em{vertices} #{V} (singular \em{vertex}) together with a set #{E} of \em{edges}, where each edge consists of a set of two vertices.}
